/-!
# Serre's theorem for coherent analytic sheaves on complex projective space

Let `P = ℙᴺ_ℂ`, let `P^an` be its analytification and `𝒪(k)^an` the analytification of the
`k`-th twisting sheaf. For a coherent analytic sheaf `𝒮` on `P^an` put
`𝒮(k) = 𝒮 ⊗ 𝒪(k)^an`. There is `k₀` such that for every `k ≥ k₀` the sheaf `𝒮(k)` is
generated by finitely many global sections and `H^q(P^an, 𝒮(k)) = 0` for every `q ≥ 1`.

The proof is the hyperplane induction of Serre. Instead of restricting to a hyperplane
`H ≅ ℙᴺ⁻¹` and inducting on `N`, all sheaves stay on `P^an`: the induction runs over sheaves
annihilated by a finite family `W` of linear forms, by descending induction on the rank of the
span of `W`, i.e. on the dimension of the linear subspace `Z(W)` supporting them. For a point
`x ∈ Z(W)` either some linear form `h` with `h(x) = 0` is independent of `W`, and the sequence
`𝒮(k - 1) → 𝒮(k) → 𝒮(k)|_H → 0` of multiplication by `h` together with the finite
dimensionality of `H¹` gives generation at `x`; or `Z(W) = {x}`, and every germ of `𝒮(k)` at `x`
extends by zero to a global section. Vanishing follows by descending induction on the degree,
starting above the uniform bound of
`MMP.Analytic.projectiveSpace_finiteDimensional_sheafCohomology`: a sheaf annihilated by `W` and
generated by global sections is built from cyclic pieces, and each cyclic piece is a quotient of
the structure sheaf `𝒪_{Z(W)}` of `Z(W)` by a coherent sheaf again annihilated by `W`.

## Main results

* `MMP.Analytic.exists_isFiniteType_generatingSections_isZero_sheafCohomology_twist`: the
  theorem above.

## Implementation notes

The tensor product is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor` over the structure sheaf of
`P^an`, the sheafification of the sectionwise tensor product. "Generated by finitely many global
sections" is the existence of a `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections` family of finite type, i.e. an
epimorphism `𝒪^n ⟶ 𝒮(k)` from a free module of finite rank given by global sections.
`H^q(P^an, -)` is the Godement cohomology `MMP.Analytic.sheafCohomology` of the underlying abelian
sheaf.

In the proof, `⊗` is the symmetric monoidal structure
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Strict.symmetricCategory`, whose tensor product is `sheafTensor` on the
nose. A sheaf
of modules is annihilated by a linear form `h` when on every standard chart `Uᵢ = {xᵢ ≠ 0}` the
holomorphic function `h / xᵢ` acts on it by zero. The family `W` is kept linearly independent.
The structure sheaf of `Z(W)` is built on `P^an` as the iterated cokernel of the multiplication
maps `𝒪_{Z(W')}(-1) → 𝒪_{Z(W')}` by the forms of `W`. Each new form is a non-zero-divisor on
`𝒪_{Z(W')}`, by Hadamard division in a chart. Hence these maps are injective, and the vanishing of
the higher cohomology of the large twists of `𝒪_{Z(W)}` follows from that of `𝒪(j)^an`, `j ≥ 0`.
On `ℙ⁰`, a point, the vanishing is the exactness of global sections.

## References

* [Serre, *Géométrie algébrique et géométrie analytique*], §14, Théorème 1
-/

@[expose] public section

